    {
        "content": "<p>I just saw this X and LinkedIn post where <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"1020114\">@Dennj Osele</span> claimed to make a new Lean compiler:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://x.com/latinumai/status/2054905760073544089?s=46\">https://x.com/latinumai/status/2054905760073544089?s=46</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://xcancel.com/latinumai/status/2054905760073544089?s=46\">https://xcancel.com/latinumai/status/2054905760073544089?s=46</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/dennjosele_lean4-formalverification-solana-ugcPost-7460657024259936256-FRQW\">https://www.linkedin.com/posts/dennjosele_lean4-formalverification-solana-ugcPost-7460657024259936256-FRQW</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>I don’t see any code however.</p>",
        "id": 595211438,
        "sender_full_name": "Jason Rute",
        "timestamp": 1778814897
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think this is the code: <a href=\"https://github.com/dennj/solana-lean\">https://github.com/dennj/solana-lean</a></p>",
        "id": 595212677,
        "sender_full_name": "Jason Rute",
        "timestamp": 1778815593
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is a cool demo and it's nice to see that you do not actually need that much to coax Lean into running on a bare metal platform.</p>\n<p>However, it's quite a bit to of an overstatement call this a new compiler. The project uses almost the exact same compilation pipeline until the step where we produce LLVM bitcode which is modified to work better for cross compilation. The bulk of the work is done in stubbing out the runtime code that would usually be platform dependent. Unfortunately here that means just disabling reference counting and reuse which is to say that the generated code will memory leak everything. In addition to that code for linear data structure like <code>Array</code> just doesn't have the uniqueness check anymore:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"C\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"nf\">lean_array_push</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">lean_array_object</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"n\">src</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">lean_array_object</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">src</span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"n\">m_capacity</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">src</span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"n\">m_size</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">src</span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"n\">m_data</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">src</span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"n\">m_size</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">lean_object</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">src</span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"n\">m_size</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">src</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"cm\">/* Grow: classic 2× expansion (with +1 floor for empty arrays). */</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">size_t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">new_cap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">src</span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"n\">m_capacity</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">src</span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"n\">m_capacity</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">lean_array_object</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"n\">dst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lean_freestanding_alloc_array</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">src</span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"n\">m_size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">new_cap</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">size_t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">src</span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"n\">m_size</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dst</span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"n\">m_data</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">src</span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"n\">m_data</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"p\">];</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">dst</span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"n\">m_data</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">src</span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"n\">m_size</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">lean_object</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dst</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>vs:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"C\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">extern</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"C\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LEAN_EXPORT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">object</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lean_array_push</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">obj_arg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">obj_arg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">object</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">lean_is_exclusive</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">lean_array_capacity</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lean_array_size</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lean_copy_expand_array</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">true</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lean_copy_expand_array_nonlinear</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lean_array_capacity</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"n\">lean_array_size</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">lean_assert</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">lean_array_capacity</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lean_array_size</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">size_t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sz</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lean_to_array</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"n\">m_size</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">object</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">**</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">it</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lean_array_cptr</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sz</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"n\">it</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">sz</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>On the one side this is a pragmatic choice as with the old code + the reference counting disabled this would just copy the array every time and cause quadratic overhead. On the other hand this means that all code which uses an array non linearly in any fashion now miscompiles and can be used to prove <code>False</code> through <code>native_decide</code>.</p>",
        "id": 595275575,
        "sender_full_name": "Henrik Böving",
        "timestamp": 1778842304
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, correct in both points. \"New compiler\" was an over-simplification for reaching a broader audience.<br>\nThe project is a demo, not production-ready. I wanted to verify the approach worked end-to-end. I still have work to do to make it ready</p>",
        "id": 595553283,
        "sender_full_name": "Dennj Osele",
        "timestamp": 1778979622
    }
]